{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user submitted a stitch task (#5101) for the go-unix-utils project to implement error handling and line numbering features in `cmd/cat`. Specifically, the task requires implementing srd006-cat requirements R1.5 (error handling), R2.1 (-n flag for numbering all lines), R2.2 (-b flag for numbering non-blank lines), and R2.3 (which the task maps to -s flag for squeezing consecutive blank lines, though the SRD's R2.3 is about -b precedence over -n). The acceptance criteria require: successful `go build`, clean `go vet`, correct -n numbering behavior, and proper stderr error output with non-zero exit on missing files. Git commands must NOT be run (managed externally by orchestrator).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU coreutils cat behavior matching (differential testing against `gcat`)\n   - Line numbering format: `%6d\\t` (right-justified width 6 + tab)\n   - Blank line definition: line containing only a newline character (R2.4)\n   - Squeeze-before-number ordering: -s applied before -n/-b (R3.3/R4.9)\n   - -b takes precedence over -n when both given (R2.3)\n   - Binary passthrough via io.Copy when no transform flags active (R1.4)\n   - Line-by-line processing with bufio.Reader.ReadBytes('\\n') for transformed output\n   - State threading (lineNum, prevBlank) across file boundaries\n   - SIGPIPE handler via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max (E8 constitution rule)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max (E9 constitution rule)\n   - Copyright header required on all Go files\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd006-cat.yaml`\n      - Read to understand full requirements. Key sections: R1 (default behavior), R2 (line numbering), R3 (blank squeezing), R4 (non-printing display - not in this task's scope), R5 (error handling/exit codes)\n      - Line number format specified: `\"%6d\\t%s\"` right-justified width 6 + tab + content\n      - Blank line = only newline char, spaces/tabs make it non-blank\n\n   - `cmd/cat/main.go` (EXISTING before modification):\n      - Had basic R1.1-R1.4 implementation from task #5100\n      - Used io.Copy for passthrough, formatErr for PathError formatting\n      - Already had SIGPIPE handler and error-to-stderr with non-zero exit\n\n   - `cmd/cat/main.go` (WRITTEN - full replacement):\n      - Added flag variables: `flagN`, `flagB`, `flagS` (package-level vars)\n      - Added `parseFlags(args []string) []string` - parses -n, -b, -s, -u flags, handles `--` end-of-flags, combined flags like `-nbs`\n      - Modified `catFile` signature to `catFile(name string, lineNum int, prevBlank bool) (int, bool, error)` - threads state across files\n      - Added `catTransform(r io.Reader, lineNum int, prevBlank bool) (int, bool, error)` - line-by-line processing with bufio\n      - Added `writeLine(w *bufio.Writer, line []byte, lineNum int, prevBlank bool) (int, bool)` - applies squeeze then number\n      - Kept `formatErr` from original\n      - Full code written:\n      ```go\n      // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n      // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n      \n      // cmd/cat implements srd006-cat: file concatenation with line numbering and blank squeezing.\n      package main\n      \n      import (\n      \t\"bufio\"\n      \t\"errors\"\n      \t\"fmt\"\n      \t\"io\"\n      \t\"os\"\n      \n      \t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n      )\n      \n      var (\n      \tflagN bool\n      \tflagB bool\n      \tflagS bool\n      )\n      \n      func main() {\n      \tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n      \targs := parseFlags(os.Args[1:])\n      \tif len(args) == 0 {\n      \t\targs = []string{\"-\"}\n      \t}\n      \texitCode := 0\n      \tlineNum := 1\n      \tprevBlank := false\n      \tfor _, name := range args {\n      \t\tvar err error\n      \t\tlineNum, prevBlank, err = catFile(name, lineNum, prevBlank)\n      \t\tif err != nil {\n      \t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"cat: %s\\n\", formatErr(err))\n      \t\t\texitCode = 1\n      \t\t}\n      \t}\n      \tif exitCode != 0 {\n      \t\tos.Exit(exitCode)\n      \t}\n      }\n      \n      func parseFlags(args []string) []string {\n      \tvar files []string\n      \tendOfFlags := false\n      \tfor _, arg := range args {\n      \t\tif endOfFlags || arg == \"\" || arg == \"-\" || arg[0] != '-' {\n      \t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n      \t\t\tcontinue\n      \t\t}\n      \t\tif arg == \"--\" {\n      \t\t\tendOfFlags = true\n      \t\t\tcontinue\n      \t\t}\n      \t\tfor _, c := range arg[1:] {\n      \t\t\tswitch c {\n      \t\t\tcase 'n':\n      \t\t\t\tflagN = true\n      \t\t\tcase 'b':\n      \t\t\t\tflagB = true\n      \t\t\tcase 's':\n      \t\t\t\tflagS = true\n      \t\t\tcase 'u':\n      \t\t\t\t// R4.8: accepted but ignored\n      \t\t\tdefault:\n      \t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"cat: invalid option -- '%c'\\n\", c)\n      \t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n      \t\t\t}\n      \t\t}\n      \t}\n      \treturn files\n      }\n      \n      func catFile(name string, lineNum int, prevBlank bool) (int, bool, error) {\n      \tvar r io.Reader\n      \tif name == \"-\" {\n      \t\tr = os.Stdin\n      \t} else {\n      \t\tf, err := os.Open(name)\n      \t\tif err != nil {\n      \t\t\treturn lineNum, prevBlank, err\n      \t\t}\n      \t\tdefer f.Close()\n      \t\tr = f\n      \t}\n      \tif !flagN && !flagB && !flagS {\n      \t\t_, err := io.Copy(os.Stdout, r)\n      \t\treturn lineNum, prevBlank, err\n      \t}\n      \treturn catTransform(r, lineNum, prevBlank)\n      }\n      \n      func catTransform(r io.Reader, lineNum int, prevBlank bool) (int, bool, error) {\n      \tbr := bufio.NewReader(r)\n      \tw := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n      \tfor {\n      \t\tline, err := br.ReadBytes('\\n')\n      \t\tif len(line) > 0 {\n      \t\t\tlineNum, prevBlank = writeLine(w, line, lineNum, prevBlank)\n      \t\t}\n      \t\tif err != nil {\n      \t\t\tif err == io.EOF {\n      \t\t\t\tbreak\n      \t\t\t}\n      \t\t\treturn lineNum, prevBlank, err\n      \t\t}\n      \t}\n      \tif ferr := w.Flush(); ferr != nil {\n      \t\treturn lineNum, prevBlank, ferr\n      \t}\n      \treturn lineNum, prevBlank, nil\n      }\n      \n      func writeLine(w *bufio.Writer, line []byte, lineNum int, prevBlank bool) (int, bool) {\n      \tisBlank := len(line) == 1 && line[0] == '\\n'\n      \tif flagS && isBlank && prevBlank {\n      \t\treturn lineNum, true\n      \t}\n      \tif (flagN || flagB) && !(flagB && isBlank) {\n      \t\tfmt.Fprintf(w, \"%6d\\t\", lineNum)\n      \t\tlineNum++\n      \t}\n      \tw.Write(line)\n      \treturn lineNum, isBlank\n      }\n      \n      func formatErr(err error) string {\n      \tvar pe *os.PathError\n      \tif errors.As(err, &pe) {\n      \t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: %s\", pe.Path, pe.Err)\n      \t}\n      \treturn err.Error()\n      }\n      ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The file was written but compilation and tests have NOT been run.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that when no transform flags are active, io.Copy should be used for binary passthrough (R1.4 preservation)\n   - Designed state threading (lineNum, prevBlank) across file boundaries to support R3.2 (squeeze across files)\n   - Implemented squeeze-before-number ordering per R3.3/R4.9\n   - Used bufio.Reader.ReadBytes('\\n') instead of bufio.Scanner to preserve newline characters in output (R1.5)\n   - Avoided `strings` import by using raw byte check `arg[0] != '-'`\n   - Handled -u flag as accepted-but-ignored per R4.8, even though not strictly in task scope, to prevent errors on valid GNU cat flags\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive tas